  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">the Government of Zimbabwe through the Zimbabwe Statistical Agency (ZMSTAT) reported on its 2019 Labour Force and Child Labour Survey (LFCLS) incorporating the 19th ICLS Resolution on statistics on work, employment and labour underutilisation.
a. Results of the 2019 LFCLS were finalized and disseminated in March 2020

The Zimbabwe Statistical Agency (ZIMSTAT) has shared the microdata with the ILO in August 2020.
 The ILO provided technical and advisory support towards the preparations for the Labour Force and Child Labour Survey

The ILO provided technical and advisory services towards the sensitisation and orientation for the ZIMSTAT technical team and the LFS Technical Committee on the 19th ICLS Resolution. The ILO also supported the development of the survey questionnaire, data analysis and report outline.</narrative>
   </description>
